  <main class="main" id="main">

    <section class="sec sec--open intro" id="top">
      <h1 class="whoami">Muhammed Ashraf Aboelsaoud</h1>
      <p class="statement">I get paid to move meaning between two languages. I do the same thing with data.</p>
      <p class="standfirst">Interpreting taught me that the hard part is never the vocabulary &mdash; it's deciding what the speaker actually meant before you open your mouth. Data is the same job. Whether an answer can be trusted is settled long before the model runs.</p>
      <p class="standfirst">I build the collection and cleaning layer that everything else sits on: pulling data out of places it was never meant to leave, giving it a shape you can query, and writing it down so the next person can repeat it.</p>
      <div class="cta">
        <a class="btn" href="mailto:muhammedaboelsaoud@gmail.com">Email me</a>
        <button class="btn btn--line" id="copy" type="button">Copy address</button>
        <a class="btn btn--line" href="https://github.com/muhammedaboelsaoud" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>
        <a class="btn btn--line" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/mohamed-aboelsaoud/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LinkedIn</a>
        <span class="copied" id="copied" role="status">Copied</span>
      </div>
      <ul class="vitals">
        <li><b>Based in</b><span>Cairo, Egypt &mdash; UTC+2, overlapping European and US mornings</span></li>
        <li><b>Studying</b><span>BSc Computer Science, Arab Open University</span></li>
        <li><b>Training</b><span>Digital Egypt Pioneers Initiative &mdash; data science and AI, team lead</span></li>
        <li><b>Working in</b><span>Python, SQL, PostgreSQL, Linux, Git</span></li>
        <li><b>Languages</b><span>Arabic and English professionally, German alongside</span></li>
        <li><b>Available for</b><span>Remote junior data roles, internships, and freelance work</span></li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="sec" id="offer">
      <div class="sec__head">
        <h2>What I take on</h2>
        <p>Four things I do well enough to be paid for. If your problem is one of these, I can start this week.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="offer">
        <div>
          <h3>Get the data out</h3>
          <p>Web pages, APIs and files that were never built to be read in bulk. I write the collector in Python, handle the pages that change shape, and hand you a table instead of a pile of tabs.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Make it clean</h3>
          <p>Deduplication, type normalisation, missing values, inconsistent naming. Every decision documented, so nobody has to guess later why a row was dropped.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Give it a schema</h3>
          <p>A PostgreSQL model with real keys and constraints, plus the queries that answer the questions you keep asking. Ask twice, get the same answer twice.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Explain it to anyone</h3>
          <p>In English or Arabic, to engineers or to the person signing off. Two years of customer-facing work and a year of teaching have made this the easy part.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============================================================
